From 996d9bd078731c0eaa65044f3ddda3a5b0684834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:58:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(rfork): adapt v0.26.0rc1 APIs and release stale MoE
 weights on fallback

Share lazy hardware profile resolution between the RFork loader and fingerprint generation, preserving legacy 310P FORCE_NZ behavior without masking unrelated import failures. Resolve the legacy MoE API and cover post-load hook restoration.

Snapshot and restore the Ascend EPLB registry during fallback. Its unconditional MoE registrations otherwise retain discarded expert weights and can exhaust NPU memory when the default loader constructs a second model. Preserve preexisting target registrations, collect partially initialized models, and avoid retaining exception tracebacks in log arguments.

Add eight regression cases using the real EPLB registry and weak references to verify discarded layers and weights are released before fallback construction. Validation: 149 CPU-isolated tests passed; Ruff, spelling and diff checks passed. Full vLLM and NPU/RDMA integration validation remains pending.

Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
